---
name: refresh-intentions
description: |-
  Daily review of each place's intention, the line saying what to do next
  there. Skips with no agent when no place changed since its last review.
steps:
  - id: review
    description: Rewrite or remove the intention of every place in the brief
    precheck:
      shells:
        - |-
          bbx engine intentions check
          # Prints the brief (per place: landmark, changes, todos, questions,
          # recent cards); exits CHECK_SKIP_CODE (75) when no place changed
          # since its last review.
      whys:
        - |-
          No need to invoke an agent when no place has a commit since its
          intention was last reviewed and no intention names a card that is
          gone.
      pass-output: true
    run:
      agents:
        - prompt: |-
            The precheck output above lists places whose `intention` needs a
            look: for each, its landmark card, the paths changed since the last
            review, its open todos, questions about its cards, and its most
            recently changed cards.

            An intention is one line on a landmark saying what the next piece
            of work in that place is, with an optional prime card (`ref`) that
            going to the place opens:

            ```yaml
            intention:
              text: "Finish the *garden post*: the trellis paragraphs are in, the ending is not"
              ref: /_content/writing/Garden_Post.doc.card
            ```

            `text` is a single non-blank line of inline Markdown. `ref` is a
            box path to an existing card in the place, or absent.

            An intention is a track the person is already on. Write one only
            from evidence of the person's choice: something they said they
            would do, a draft they were editing, a todo or question of theirs,
            or the standing job of a place that exists to process what arrives
            (its `destinations` rules say so). A card merely being present,
            incomplete, or newly arrived is not an intention, and work the
            person set aside on purpose is not either. With no such evidence,
            remove the field. The intention is "what next"; the landmark body
            stays "where things stand".

            For each listed place, rewrite, keep, or remove its `intention`.
            Prefer the current line's wording when it still holds. When its
            `ref` names a card that is gone, point it at the card the work now
            happens in or drop `ref`.

            EDIT ONLY the `intention` field of the listed landmarks. Do not
            touch any other field, the body, or any other card: the validate
            step fails the run on any other change.

            Changing nothing is a normal outcome: say so and do not commit.
            Otherwise stage only the landmarks you edited, by explicit path,
            and commit:

            ```bash
            git add -- <each landmark path you edited> && git commit -m "$(cat <<'MSG'
            Intentions: <the places, by name>

            <one line per place: what changed and why>

            Created-By: refresh-intentions
            MSG
            )"
            ```

            Do NOT add Co-Authored-By.
          max-turns: 15
    validate:
      shells:
        - bbx engine intentions verify
      whys:
        - |-
          The review record is what keeps a place off tomorrow's list; it
          must not be written over an edit outside the listed intentions, or
          over landmark edits left uncommitted.
      severity: abort
---
